From 3f8223d50b560eece75d128e1b139c6f7252c462 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mustafa Senoglu <mmustafasenoglu0@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:41:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/tools: fix wrong new-file start line in unified diff

Fixes #81453

When toUnified joins a nearby edit into the current hunk it adds the intervening lines without advancing the new-file counter, so every later hunk header gets a stale start line. One-line fix, verified against the reproducer in the issue (output now matches GNU diff).

Change-Id: I205ce03db5e6db043bec0e3654ef6eb5809a8e46
GitHub-Last-Rev: e135a42156aede7624b869cd526ad7cd75859084
GitHub-Pull-Request: golang/go#81588
---

diff --git a/internal/diff/unified.go b/internal/diff/unified.go
index 6e8adad..aeeb49f 100644
--- a/internal/diff/unified.go
+++ b/internal/diff/unified.go
@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@
 			//direct extension
 		case h != nil && start <= last+gap:
 			//within range of previous lines, add the joiners
-			addEqualLines(h, lines, last, start)
+			toLine += addEqualLines(h, lines, last, start)
 		default:
 			//need to start a new hunk
 			if h != nil {
